## 20. Readiness contracts — SPEC-A3

The user-approved 2026-09-26 readiness decisions authorize this section (8B-02–08/11). It completes §§5/7/8/9 without changing the existing Command/Receipt or provider schema contracts, pixel rules, one-active-request default, full-history policy or PERF ceilings. The route and policy inventory is mirrored in [readiness-contracts.json](readiness-contracts.json); the consumer oracles are [TEST §13](testing.md#s13). This is a specified protocol, not evidence of an implemented or qualified server.

### 20.1 Local protocol LP-1

All paths below are under /api/v1. JSON is UTF-8, duplicate keys, unknown properties/discriminators, nonfinite numbers, unpaired surrogates and unsupported protocolVersion rejected before command acceptance. ProtocolVersion is 1; unsupported major version returns 426 PROTOCOL_VERSION with supportedVersions:[1]. IDs are opaque bounded strings (1–128 ASCII letters/digits/underscore/hyphen); sequences, revisions, offsets and lengths are canonical unsigned decimal strings, including "0", never floating-point counters. Content bytes use separate streaming routes. JSON control envelopes are ≤64KiB, event rows ≤16KiB; large details/manifests/provenance stay referenced blobs. Oversized metadata returns 413 without truncating user input.

Canonical command hash LP-1: parse with duplicate detection; validate the §5.2 Command shape and typed body; hash the UTF-8 encoding of {protocolVersion:1,command:Command}. Recursively sort object keys by Unicode scalar value, preserve array order and string code points (no Unicode/newline normalization); encode strings with JSON quotation, escaping quote/backslash and controls U+0000–001F (lowercase four-digit \\u escapes), leaving other scalar values literal. Numbers use ECMAScript JSON.stringify finite binary64 representation (negative zero becomes 0); identities requiring exact large integers already use decimal strings. Omitted optional keys stay omitted; null is distinct. Include every envelope field, body and BlobRef identity/hash/length; do not include HTTP headers, cookie, CSRF token or whitespace. Store original validated envelope plus hash. ClientId/sessionId are immutable command provenance, not current authentication: a renewed session can query/resend its authorized original envelope unchanged. Same ID/different hash is HTTP 409 COMMAND_ID_REUSE with no receipt overwrite or effect, even after restart. Validation must not fetch arbitrary client URLs.

