| --- | --- | --- |
| Hostile website or DNS rebinding | Exact launch Host+port, exact Origin whenever present; mutations require Origin. Reject null Origin and cross-site fetch metadata; no Access-Control-Allow-Origin | SEC01 foreign/rebound/IPv6-alias Host, null Origin and forged forwarded headers yield zero state/provider effects |
| Missing Origin on normal browser navigation/media | Authenticated GET/HEAD immutable content may omit Origin with Sec-Fetch-Site:same-origin and scoped authorization. JSON GET and fetch-based SSE may omit Origin only with those checks plus X-App-Client:LP-1. Static shell is session-free but contains no secrets. Mutations never permit absent Origin | SEC02 anonymous/cross-site content and absent-Origin API without client marker rejected; authenticated same-origin browser reads succeed |
| Pairing theft/replay, session fixation | Fragment-only one-use expiring token; cookie/token rotation; no token in logs/events/bundles; bootstrap is only unauthenticated API | SEC03 expired/reused token, revoked session, old CSRF and restart fail without effect |
| Sensitive data via GET/stream | Same session/scope checks as commands; no-store API/provenance; safety status enforced at asset endpoint, including ranges/thumbnails | SEC04 blocked/unknown-safety bytes cannot bypass UI through direct URL/range |
| Untrusted project/prompt/file text | Render text as text; never insert HTML or execute supplied code; CSP default-src 'self', object-src 'none', frame-ancestors 'none', base-uri 'none'; restrict connect-src to exact local origin, images to self/blob, fonts and workers to app resources | SEC05 hostile filename/prompt/archive renders inert; signed URLs never become browser src |
